:: School Blindfold Hallway
<<set $daily.blindfoldHall to true>>
<<if blindAdaptationStrength() >= 1>>
	As you walk down the school hallway, you hear someone opening a locker nearby. The metal door makes a noise as it opens, and you realise it is blocking part of your path. You move to one side and walk past without hitting it.
	<br><br>
	"How did you know that was there?" a student asks behind you. You hear the student walking closer, apparently surprised that you managed to avoid the door while wearing a blindfold.
<<else>>
	"Can you actually see through that?" a student asks as you walk past.
	<br><br>
	Before you can answer, another student grabs your sleeve and stops you from walking forward.
	"Careful! There's an open locker right in front of you."
	<br><br>
	You realise you were about to walk into its door.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if C.npc.Robin.state is "active" and C.npc.Robin.love gte 50 and getRobinLocation() is "school">>
	<<set $phase to "Robin">><<npc Robin>><<person1>>
	You recognise Robin's voice calling your name from nearby. <<He>> comes closer so you can hear <<him>> clearly.
	"It's me! Do you want to hold my arm? I can help you get through the hallway."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Take Robin's arm|School Blindfold Hallway Help]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<<elseif C.npc.Kylar.state is "active" and C.npc.Kylar.love gte 50 and Time.schoolTime>>
	<<set $phase to "Kylar">><<npc Kylar>><<person1>>
	Another student walks past you and accidentally bumps into your shoulder.
	<br><br>
	"W-Watch where you're going!" Kylar shouts at the student.
	<<He>> then comes closer to you and speaks more quietly. "I can walk with you, if you want."
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Let Kylar guide you|School Blindfold Hallway Help]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<<else>>
	<<set $phase to "student">>
	A student stays beside you while the other students continue walking down the hallway.
	<br><br>
	<<link [[Ask the student to guide you|School Blindfold Hallway Help]]>><<pass 1>><</link>>
	<br>
<</if>>
<<link [[Continue on your own|School Blindfold Hallway Alone]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: School Blindfold Hallway Help
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<if $phase is "Robin">>
	You reach out, and Robin offers <<his>> arm for you to hold. Once you have a good grip, <<he>> starts walking slowly beside you.
	<br><br>
	"There's a bag on the floor to your left," <<he>> tells you. "Stay close to me. We'll walk around it."
	<br><br>
	You follow Robin through the crowded hallway, holding <<his>> arm while <<he>> helps you avoid the other students and their bags.
	<br><br>
	When you reach the next classroom, Robin stops. You use your free hand to touch the side of the classroom door so you know where you are, then let go of <<his>> arm.
<<elseif $phase is "Kylar">>
	You hold out your hand, waiting for Kylar to help you. <<He>> hesitates for a moment before offering <<his>> arm. You hold onto it, and <<he>> starts walking beside you.
	<br><br>
	"There's a bag on the floor ahead. M-Move a little to the right," <<he>> tells you.
	<br><br>
	Kylar walks on the side where most of the other students are passing, helping you avoid bumping into anyone. <<He>> also walks slowly so you can keep up.
	<br><br>
	When you reach the next classroom, you let go of <<his>> arm. <<He>> stays beside you for a moment before finally moving away.
<<else>>
	You ask the student to help you get through the crowded hallway. The student offers an arm, and you hold onto it.
	<br><br>
	The student walks beside you, helping you avoid the other students and the bags left on the floor.
	<br><br>
	When you reach the next classroom, you let go of the student's arm and thank them for helping you.
<</if>>
<<stress -2>><<lstress>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Hallways]]>><<endevent>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: School Blindfold Hallway Alone
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
"No thanks. I'll walk on my own," you say.
<br><br>
<<if $phase is "Robin">>
	"All right. See you later," Robin says before walking away.
<<elseif $phase is "Kylar">>
	"Oh. O-Okay," Kylar says. <<He>> moves away from you, leaving you enough space to continue walking.
<<else>>
	"All right. Just be careful," the student says before walking away.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if blindAdaptationStrength() >= 1>>
	You listen to the footsteps and voices of the students around you. Even though you can't see them, you can tell where most of them are walking.
	<br><br>
	You follow behind the other students, keeping some distance so you don't bump into anyone. When you hear locker doors opening nearby, you move farther away from the lockers and continue down the hallway.
<<else>>
	You place one hand against the lockers to help you find your way. Since you can't see where you're going, you have to move slowly.
	<br><br>
	When you reach an open locker door, you stop and carefully walk around it before continuing. It takes you longer than usual, but you manage to get through the hallway without hitting anything else.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Hallways]]>><<endevent>><<set $eventskip to 1>><</link>>
<br>

:: School Blindfold Classroom
<<set $daily.blindfoldClass to true>>
<<set _blindfoldTeacher to {science: "Sirris", maths: "River", english: "Doren", history: "Winter", housekeeping: "River"}[$phase]>>
_blindfoldTeacher pauses beside your desk.
"Can you still do your schoolwork while wearing that blindfold?"
<br><br>
<<if blindAdaptationStrength() >= 1>>
	You reach across your desk and find your school supplies without any trouble, even though you can't see them. A few students sitting behind you begin whispering to each other after hearing the question.
<<else>>
	You move your hands across the desk, trying to find your school supplies. You accidentally push a pencil towards the edge of the desk, but manage to stop it before it falls onto the floor.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<link [[Ask for help following the lesson|School Blindfold Classroom Help]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Say you can manage|School Blindfold Classroom Alone]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: School Blindfold Classroom Help
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<set _blindfoldTeacher to {science: "Sirris", maths: "River", english: "Doren", history: "Winter", housekeeping: "River"}[$phase]>>
"Could you explain what you're doing?" you ask. "I can't see the demonstration."
<br><br>
_blindfoldTeacher pauses and agrees. When the next demonstration begins, <<nnpc_he _blindfoldTeacher>> explains each step while doing it, describing what is happening at the front of the classroom.
<br><br>
You listen carefully and find it much easier to follow the lesson now that you don't need to see what _blindfoldTeacher is doing.
<<stress -2>><<lstress>>
<br><br>
<<set _blindfoldLessonReturn to {science: "Science Lesson", maths: "Maths Lesson", english: "English Lesson", history: "History Lesson", housekeeping: "Housekeeping Lesson"}[$phase] || "Hallways">>
<<link "Next" _blindfoldLessonReturn>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: School Blindfold Classroom Alone
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<set _blindfoldTeacher to {science: "Sirris", maths: "River", english: "Doren", history: "Winter", housekeeping: "River"}[$phase]>>
"I can manage," you tell _blindfoldTeacher.
<br><br>
_blindfoldTeacher waits while you put your school supplies on the desk, keeping them close enough to find without looking. Once you're ready, <<nnpc_he _blindfoldTeacher>> continues the lesson.
<br><br>
<<if blindAdaptationStrength() >= 1>>
	You're already used to wearing the blindfold, so you can follow _blindfoldTeacher's instructions and continue your classwork without much trouble.
<<else>>
	You have trouble finding what you need while wearing the blindfold. You use your hands to check where your things are, then listen carefully to _blindfoldTeacher's instructions. It's harder to keep up with the lesson, but you manage to begin the classwork without asking for help.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<set _blindfoldLessonReturn to {science: "Science Lesson", maths: "Maths Lesson", english: "English Lesson", history: "History Lesson", housekeeping: "Housekeeping Lesson"}[$phase] || "Hallways">>
<<link "Next" _blindfoldLessonReturn>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>

:: Events Shades Remove
<<set $outside to 1>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
You reach up and take the $worn.face.name off yourself before <<he>> can.
<br><br>
River stops short, hand half-raised, and lowers it. "...Thank you."
<<He>> sounds almost disappointed to have nothing to confiscate. "See that they stay off."
<br><br>
The watching students lose interest and drift away, disappointed there was nothing to watch.
<br><br>
<<if !$settings.blindStatsEnabled>>
	<span class="blue">You put your $worn.face.name away yourself.</span>
	<br><br>
<</if>>
<<status -3>><<npcincr River dom 1>><<npcincr River love 1>><<lcool>>
<<generalUndress "wardrobe" "face">>
<<courtyard>>

:: Events Shades Excuse
<<set $outside to 1>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<shadesExcuseDifficulty 600>>
<<shadesExcuseLine>>
<br><br>
<<shadesExcuseCheck>>
<br><br>
<<if $skulduggerysuccess is 1>>
	River studies you for a long moment. "...Is that documented with the infirmary?"
	<br><br>
	You hold <<his>> gaze. Eventually <<he>> exhales through <<his>> nose. "Then see that it is.
	I don't want to have this conversation twice." <<He>> marches away,
	and the watching students look faintly impressed that you got away with it.
	<br><br>
	<span class="green">You keep your $worn.face.name.</span><<status 2>><<gcool>>
<<else>>
	River doesn't even blink. "Sensitive eyes," <<he>> repeats. "How convenient."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> holds out <<his>> hand and waits, and the waiting is worse than shouting.
	<span class="red">You hand them over.</span>
	<br><br>
	"Lying to a member of staff. I'll see you in detention." <<He>> marches away with your $worn.face.name.
	<br><br>
	<<generatey2>>A <<person2>><<person>> winces on your behalf.
	<<status -10>><<gtrauma>><<trauma 6>><<detention 3>><<llcool>><<gdelinquency>>
	<<generalUndress "wardrobe" "face">>
<</if>>
<<courtyard>>


:: Sydney Chat Shades Remove
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<run statusCheck("Sydney")>>
You take the $worn.face.name off without being asked twice.
<br><br>
Sydney brightens, visibly relieved not to have had to push.
"Thank you. I know it's a silly rule, but it isn't mine to bend."
<<npcincr Sydney love 1>><<npcincr Sydney purity 1>><<glove>><<gspurity>>
<<generalUndress "wardrobe" "face">>
<br><br>
<<sydneyOptions>>


:: Sydney Chat Shades Excuse
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "school">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<run statusCheck("Sydney")>>
<<shadesExcuseDifficulty 400>>
<<shadesExcuseLine>>
<br><br>
<<shadesExcuseCheck>>
<br><br>
<<if $skulduggerysuccess is 1>>
	"Oh." Sydney's face falls immediately. "Oh, I'm sorry, I didn't... that's completely different, then."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> fidgets with <<his>> own <<sydneyGlasses>>, embarrassed.
	"I shouldn't have assumed. I'll say something if anyone else brings it up."
	<br><br>
	<span class="green">You keep your $worn.face.name,</span> and feel slightly bad about it.<<status 2>><<gcool>>
<<else>>
	Sydney looks at you for a moment too long.
	<br><br>
	"You don't wear them anywhere else," <<he>> says quietly. "Not on the way to school and at the shops."
	<<He>> doesn't sound angry, which is somehow worse. "Please just take them off."
	<br><br>
	<span class="red">You take them off.</span><<gstress>><<stress 6>><<npcincr Sydney love -2>><<llove>>
	<<generalUndress "wardrobe" "face">>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<sydneyOptions>>

:: School Changing Room Cameras
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "pool">><<schooleffects>><<effects>>
<<set $weekly.lockerCamerasSabotaged to true>>
You return to the places where the photographs must have been taken: the vent above the showers, the clock on the wall,
and the smoke detector above the benches. You check each one carefully,
looking for anything that could hide a small camera.
<br><br>
<<if $skulduggerysuccess is 1>>
	Behind each cover, you find a small lens with wires leading into the wall.
	You open them one by one, pull the wires free from each camera, then put the covers back into place.
	<br><br>
	From the changing room, they look the same as they did before.
	<span class="green">None of the cameras can record anything now.</span>
	<br><br>
	Leighton will probably notice eventually and replace them within a week.<<llstress>><<stress -6>>
	<<if $leightonCameraSuspicion isnot "exposed">><<set $leightonCameraSuspicion to "clean">><</if>>
<<else>>
	You find the cameras hidden in the vent and smoke detector first, then remove their wires.
	The last one takes longer to find. After checking around the clock,
	you discover another small camera hidden behind it.
	<br><br>
	As you reach towards it, a red light appears beside the lens.
	You realise the camera has already started recording you. <span class="red">It saw you trying to remove it.</span>
	<br><br>
	You pull its wires free anyway and put the clock back, but whoever checks the recording may already know what you did.
	<<ggstress>><<stress 7>>
	<<set $leightonCameraSuspicion to "exposed">>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<skulduggeryuse 500>>
<<destination_pool>>

:: Shades Excuse Widgets [widget]
/*
	Pure calculation. <<shadesExcuseCheck>> updates the counter.
	Recheck before the roll because $skulduggerydifficulty can be outdated.
*/
<<widget "shadesExcuseDifficulty">>
	<<set _base to (_args[0] ?? 500)>>
	<<set _englishHelp to Math.floor(($english ?? 0) / 5)>>
	<<set _excuseUses to ($daily.shadesExcuseUses ?? 0)>>
	<<set $skulduggerydifficulty to Math.clamp(_base - _englishHelp + (_excuseUses * 150), 100, 1000)>>
<</widget>>

<<widget "shadesExcuseCheck">>
	<<set $daily.shadesExcuseUses to ($daily.shadesExcuseUses ?? 0) + 1>>
	<<skulduggerycheck>>
	<<if $skulduggerysuccess is 1>>
		<<skulduggery 3>>
	<<else>>
		<<skulduggery 1>>
	<</if>>
<</widget>>

/* The excuse itself, phrased to attitude. Shared by both call-out sites. */
<<widget "shadesExcuseLine">>
	<<speechresolve>>
	<<switch _speechAttitudeResolved>>
		<<case "meek" "shy">>
			"M-My eyes are sensitive," you say, not quite looking at <<him>>. "The light hurts."
		<<case "polite" "docile">>
			"I'm sorry," you say. "My eyes are sensitive to light. I'd rather keep them on, if that's alright."
		<<case "flamboyant">>
			"Delicate eyes, darling," you say, touching the frames. "The strip lighting in here is an assault."
		<<case "bratty" "cruel">>
			"They're for my eyes," you say flatly. "Which are sensitive. Unless you'd like to explain that to a doctor."
		<<case "confident">>
			"Sensitive eyes," you say. "Bright light gives me headaches. That's the whole story."
		<<default>>
			"My eyes are sensitive to light," you say. "That's all it is."
	<</switch>>
<</widget>>